# Cursor AI Rules (.cursorrules)

# Project Context
This is a high-standard Python Coding, Data Structures & Algorithms, PyTorch AI Deep Learning, and SQL Practice repository.

# Coding Guidelines
- Language: Python 3.10+ / 3.11+
- Always write type hints on function signatures: def func(a: int, b: list) -> int:
- Preserve docstrings with markdown formatting, complexity notes (Time: O(N), Space: O(1)), and input/expected examples.
- Include standard cell markers `# %% [markdown]` and `# %% [code]` in interactive learning scripts.
- Never write destructive file overwrite operations unless explicitly instructed.
- When adding new questions to `python_interview_patterns/`, register them in the `TESTS` dictionary with proper test inputs and expected outputs.
- When generating PyTorch models, support both CPU and GPU (`device = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'`).

# Running Commands
- Test all cells: python <file.py> --all
- Test single cell: python <file.py> <cell_number>
- Run DSA Pattern: python python_interview_patterns/<topic>/<topic>.py [q_num]
- Run PyTorch AI Module: python AI/<tier>/<module>.py
